ROLE: SECONDARY_REVIEWER. Codex is PRIMARY. Read-only independent review; no edits, implementation, Codex invocation or delegation. Return VERDICT (PASS or CHANGES_REQUESTED), SUMMARY, evidence-backed FINDINGS P0-P3, tests/risks, recommended actions, confidence according to embedded protocol.
Bounded security change: revoke EXECUTE on exposed SECURITY DEFINER helper public._sync_contrato_titulares(uuid,jsonb), owner postgres, which deletes/reinserts public.contrato_titulares but does not authenticate or authorize. Existing ACL: postgres,anon,authenticated,service_role each explicit EXECUTE. Actual synthetic copied database test: SET ROLE anon with empty JWT successfully replaced titulars on an unfrozen contract, then ROLLBACK. Frozen PDF trigger protects immutability only, not permission.
Existing callers public.crear_contrato and public.actualizar_contrato are SECURITY DEFINER owner postgres. They check actor and permissions before calling helper. Seven real SQL role/claims test groups after exact REVOKE: three API roles denied direct helper calls (42501), authorized creation with titular succeeds, authorized editing titular succeeds, canonical create/update reject no session, frozen PDF contract still rejects edits(55000). Existing bodies unchanged; bank-original unchanged. No production mutations.
CodeGraph attempted first; no .codegraph in worktree. pg_proc body inventory found only those two callers. Focused frontend/edge search found comments and generated types, no direct helper invocations. This is not comprehensive external-client telemetry.
Module will be appended to final candidate and separately installed only in synthetic bank with identity then F4 exclusive locks, F4 OFF, all37candidate bodies checked unchanged. Final candidate not yet deployed or versioned. Neutral cotitular links are a separate pending feature, irrelevant to this ACL prerequisite.
Questions: Is revoking PUBLIC + all three API grants sufficient? Any evidenced regression despite successful canonical paths? Drift guard or permission issue? Avoid speculative broad audits. Primary consulted PG17 docs: SECURITY DEFINER executes with owner privileges, default PUBLIC execute should be revoked atomically.

